                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 57-year-old male admitted on 01/03/2012 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced exercise tolerance. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed significant airflow obstruction with hypoxaemia. Spirometry supported the diagnosis of severe COPD. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive intravenous fluids. He responded well to treatment with marked symptomatic improvement. Patient education regarding inhaler technique and disease self-management was provided prior to discharge. Please arrange follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Discharge medication and further recommendations are enclosed. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>
               </text>
